    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d233">

                <pb facs="0427" n="337" sameAs="frus:frus1932v02/pg337"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.11W892/2157</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The German Ambassador (Von Prittwitz) to the Secretary
                            of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-12-30">December 30, 1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: I have the honor to
                    transmit to Your Excellency herewith two communications<anchor n="67"
                        xml:id="d233-f1"/> of this date addressed to the Secretary of the Treasury
                    of the United States, with the request that you will be good enough to forward
                    them to the Secretary of the Treasury.</p>
                <p>In these communications I have declared to the Treasury Department of the United
                    States, acting under instructions from my Government, in accordance with
                    Sections 5 and 8 of the German-American Debt Funding Agreement of June 23, 1930,
                    that Germany will postpone the payments falling due on March 31, 1933 under
                    Sections 1<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi> and 1<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi> of
                    the said agreement, for the claims allowed by the <pb facs="0428" n="338"
                        xml:id="pg338"/> German-American Mixed Commission and for the amounts due
                    for compensation for the costs, in arrears, of the American Army of
                    Occupation.</p>
                <p>With the renewed assurance [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. von
                                Prittwitz</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
